  "notes": "{要|い}る is a godan verb meaning \"to need\" or \"to require.\"\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xが{要|い}る: X is needed\n- Xが{要|い}らない: X is not needed\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {要|い}る (godan, \"need\"): ends in -ru but conjugates as godan\n- いる (ichidan, \"exist\"): animate existence verb\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {時間|じかん}が{要|い}る (time is needed)\n- お{金|かね}が{要|い}る (money is needed)\n- {要|い}らない (I don't need it)\n\nNOTE: Often written in kana as いる, but context distinguishes it from the existence verb.",
